// Capture: an anonymous function reading a name from the function that
// encloses it.
//
// This is what makes an anonymous function a closure rather than a lifted
// function, and it does not work. parseexpr.c lifts the declaration to module
// scope as it parses it, so by the time names are resolved the body is no
// longer inside 'scaleAll' and 'factor' is not a name it can see. Name
// resolution reports ErrorUnkName and the compile exits 1.
//
// The scenario is written as the code that should work rather than as an
// assertion of the failure, and marked xfail, so that it starts failing the
// suite the day capture lands rather than quietly enshrining the gap. It fails
// cleanly -- a diagnostic and exit 1, not a miscompile -- which is what makes
// xfail honest here.
//
// Nothing is called and there is no 'main': the point is whether this compiles
// at all, so the category is 'compile'.

fn scaleAll(factor i32, v i32) i32 {
  imm scale = &fn(x i32) i32 {x * factor}
  scale(v)
}
